# Environment variables — names only. Copy what you need; never commit real values.
#
# There are two separate consumers in this project, and they do not read the same file:
#
#   1. The client bundle (Vite). Anything prefixed `VITE_` is inlined into the JavaScript
#      shipped to the browser at build time, so it is public by definition. Only put a
#      value here if you would be happy to see it in the page source.
#   2. The Strava token exchange (`functions/api/strava/token.js`, a Cloudflare Pages
#      Function). It reads `STRAVA_CLIENT_ID` / `STRAVA_CLIENT_SECRET` from its own
#      environment: the Pages project's variables in production, and a `.dev.vars` file
#      (gitignored) when running `wrangler pages dev` locally.
#
# Setup steps and what each variable is for: docs/STRAVA-SETUP.md

# --- Client (Vite) -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Enables the demo seed data in a production build. Dev builds always seed, so this is
# only for running the E2E suite against demo content deliberately (see
# `DEMO_SEEDING_ENABLED` in src/lib/data/seed.ts). Harmless: it is a flag, not a secret.
VITE_SEED_DEMO=

# The Strava application's Client ID. It appears in the authorize URL the rider is sent
# to, so it is not a secret — which is exactly why the *secret* must never be given this
# prefix: `VITE_` values end up in the bundle.
VITE_STRAVA_CLIENT_ID=

# --- Strava token exchange (Pages Function / `.dev.vars`) ---------------------------
# Read only by functions/api/strava/token.js. Set both on the Pages project
# (Production **and** Preview) — see docs/STRAVA-SETUP.md.
STRAVA_CLIENT_ID=
# NEVER prefix this with `VITE_`. The whole point of the Function is that the secret stays
# on the server; the browser must never receive it.
STRAVA_CLIENT_SECRET=
